cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or data, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Code and data for: Calibration-based predictions versus measured logical errors for heavy-hex memories on IBM Fez"
abstract: >-
  Code and data for a comparison on IBM Fez of the heavy-hex subsystem code
  at distances 3 and 5, run side by side, with a noise model built from IBM's
  published calibration. Predictions were stored before each job. The paper
  compares these forecasts with measured failure probabilities using the same
  decoder on device and simulated shots. The forecasts underpredict the early-depth
  logical errors, and distance 5 performs worse than distance 3 on these
  implementations. The repository contains the fifteen jobs' calibrations,
  circuits, predictions, shots and analyses, the paper's post-run comparisons,
  and the IBM Kingston follow-up experiments.
